<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>IOS on Antoine Boucher</title><link>http://localhost:1313/blog/tags/ios/</link><description>Recent content in IOS on Antoine Boucher</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 02 Jan 2024 10:00:00 -0400</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="http://localhost:1313/blog/tags/ios/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>LiDAR apartment scan with Rhino on iPhone</title><link>http://localhost:1313/blog/posts/rhino-lidar-apartment-scan/</link><pubDate>Tue, 02 Jan 2024 10:00:00 -0400</pubDate><guid>http://localhost:1313/blog/posts/rhino-lidar-apartment-scan/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="introduction"&gt;Introduction&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We used the Rhino app on an iPhone with LiDAR to scan our apartment and make clearer decisions about layout and furniture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="lidar-and-rhino"&gt;LiDAR and Rhino&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;LiDAR captures depth quickly; Rhino on iPhone turns those scans into workable 3D geometry for review on device.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="process"&gt;Process&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We walked room by room while the phone mapped space; Rhino updated the model as we moved.&lt;/p&gt;
